 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased
+
+- Added explicit Paperclip-managed ACP startup with immutable assigned instructions, prompt, workspace, tool schemas, and exact `openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol` subscription admission over restricted IPC. Managed sessions do not load local credentials, discovery settings, client MCP servers, or prior conversations.
+- Isolated managed Python and shell descendants in a nested bubblewrap namespace without the worker's broker socket, manifest, or parent process view. Managed startup requires an offline, prebuilt Python runtime.
+- Fenced managed compaction, refinement, branch navigation, child sessions, model changes, and autonomous continuation. Cancellation and approval observation retain pending ownership until authoritative broker receipts; uncertain effects are never redispatched.
+- Serialized managed MCP tool batches so each governed effect retains the operation's single owner until its authoritative result, including approval waits. Managed kernel roots also exclude `/etc` and `/sys`.
+
 ## [0.9.7] - 2026-09-28
 
 - Changed the continual-harness kernel surface back to the twelve per-kind CRUD methods on `rlm.harness` (`create_memory`/`update_memory`/`delete_memory` plus the `*_skill`, `*_subagent`, and `*_prompt_note` methods), the `path` spelling of the harness entry grouping, and callable `rlm.harness.record_refinement`/`plan_refinement`, reverting #2154 and #2155 at the user's request.
